"""Capability tokens — unforgeable, linear, revocable.

A capability is a (resource, permissions, nonce) triple.
Capabilities cannot be forged (nonce is cryptographic).
Capabilities are linear (transfer consumes the original).
Capabilities can be attenuated (reduce permissions, never increase).
Capabilities can be revoked (invalidate by nonce).

Reference: Dennis & Van Horn, "Programming Semantics for
Multiprogrammed Computations" (1966).
Biblical: Matthew 25:14-30 — Parable of the Talents.
Each servant receives capabilities proportional to trust.
